[8403]="7000B0DD\n1\tBring the mathoms to Greylond Bottomley\030Collect mathoms (total: 10)\tGreylond Bottomley is at the Mathom House in Michel Delving in the Shire. Greylond Bottomley has asked you to bring him any mathoms that you gather during your travels. Mathoms drop off of Men, Dwarves, Orc-kind, Troll-kind, and the Dead of level 35 - 45 throughout the world.\n",
[8404]="70030445\n1\tDefeat the Warg-matron\tA great matron to the Wargs of the Howling Wood has settled near the abandoned worksite.\n2\tDefeat the Warg-matron\tWargs have recently moved into the work site to the east of Floodwend.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated the Warg-matron of the Howling Wood.\n",
[8405]="700346C0\n1\tDefeat Gajat, the Warg-matron\tThe Warg-matron's den is in the south-west corner of Edsig's Farm. She can be found lurking near the small barn.\n2\tDefeat Gajat, the Warg-matron\tThe Warg-matron, Gajat, lurks outside a small barn that is now her den. This den is in the south-west corner of Edsig's Farm.\n3\tReturn to Oter\tOter is awaiting your return at Thrymm's Farm and will be happy to know of what you accomplished while at Edsig's Farm.\n",
[8406]="7006218A\n1\tDefeat Grodris, the matron of the Wintersebb\tGrodris, the matron of the Wintersebb, now stalks the Isendeep mine in the Ettenmoors. Destroy her, and earn power for your side of the battle.\n2\tDefeat Grodris, the matron of the Wintersebb\tGrodris, the matron of the Wintersebb, now stalks the mountains of the Ettenmoors. If left unchecked, there is no telling what this unbound beast will do to Orc and Elf alike. Destroy her.\n",
[8407]="7006460F\n1\tDefeat Grodris, the matron of the Wintersebb\tGrodris, the matron of the Wintersebb, now stalks the Isendeep mine in the Ettenmoors. Destroy her and earn power for your side of the battle.\n2\tDefeat Grodris, the matron of the Wintersebb\tGrodris, the matron of the Wintersebb, now stalks the mountains of the Ettenmoors. If left unchecked, there is no telling what this unbound beast will do to Orc and Elf alike. Destroy her.\n",
[8408]="7005C411\n1\tTalk to Klátha\tKlátha is located in a camp north of Bazanmanar. Nósni has asked you to bring the furs to Klátha.\n2\tAdd furs to the pile\tThe pile of furs is next to Klátha, in northern Clovengap. You should add your furs to the pile.\n3\tSpeak to Klátha\tKlátha is located in Bazanmanar. You should let Klátha know you have added your furs to the pile.\n4\tReturn to Nósni\tNósni is located in a camp north of Bazanmanar. Klátha has asked you to give her message of refusal to Nósni.\n",
[8409]="7005D3B7\n1\tTalk to Mother Amma\tMother Amma is located in Bazanmanar. Nósni has asked you to ask Mother Amma whether she knows why Klátha is angry.\n2\tReturn to Nósni\tNósni is located in a camp north of Bazanmanar. You should let Nósni know what Mother Amma said.\n",
[8410]="700395D4\n1\tThe traders' pavillion can be found to the south of the Mead Hall of Middlemead. Mágla has asked you to take inventory of currently stocked goods in Middlemead. You can find these goods amongst the traders in Middlemead.\t\n2\tTalk to Hildulf\tHildulf can be found on the raised platform at the traders' pavillion. You have noted the stock of Middlemead and should now speak to Hildulf.\n3\tCollect Hildulf's manifest\tThe manifest can be found near Hildulf in the traders' pavillion of Middlemead. You have spoken to Hildulf and should now take the manifest and return to Mágla.\n4\tTalk to Thane Mágla\tMágla can be found inside the Mead Hall of Middlemead. You have obtained Hildulf's manifest and should now present it to Thane Mágla.\n",
[8411]="7000C382\n1\tTalk to Aeglas at his cell in the Goblin-town prison\tAeglas is in his cell in the Goblin-town prison. Oghûk told you that the goblin-torturer Matuga has the key to his cell secured on a loop on his belt. Something in Oghûk's voice is disconcerting, however. You should return to Aeglas.\n2\tReturn the key to Aeglas at his cell in the Goblin-town prison\030Collect Jail Key\tMatuga is on the way to the Great Goblin's throne-room at the centre of Goblin-town. Aeglas distrusts the goblin Oghûk's intentions, but he does not doubt that the goblin believes that the key is with the torturer. Aeglas agrees that you must search the paths on the way to the Great Goblin's throne-room for Matuga and the key.\n",
[8412]="70054805\n1\tDefeat armoured shadows at Matum Graz\tMatum Graz can be found in Emyn Duir. You should defeat armoured shadows at Matum Graz.\n2\tDefeat armoured shadows at Matum Graz (total: 10)\tMatum Graz can be found in Emyn Duir. You should defeat armoured shadows at Matum Graz.\n3\tCompleted\tDefeated many armoured shadows at Matum Graz.\n",
[8413]="70054806\n1\tDestroy weapon racks at Matum Graz\tMatum Graz can be found in Emyn Duir. You should destroy weapon racks at Matum Graz.\n2\tDestroy spear racks at Matum Graz (total: 8)\030Destroy sword racks at Matum Graz (total: 8)\tMatum Graz can be found in Emyn Duir. You should destroy weapon racks at Matum Graz.\n3\tCompleted\tDestroyed many weapons racks at Matum Graz.\n",
[8414]="7002F899\n1\tDefeat Uruk-hai at Kufuzg (total: 10)\tMany Uruk-hai have attempted to establish an encampment south of Elthengels at Kufuzg. Defeat the Uruk-hai who reside at Kufuzg and help put an end to the Uruk-leader's threat.\n2\tReturn to the Guard-captain at the trader's outpost\tThe Guard-captain of the merchants can be found at the trader's outpost, along the road west of Elthengels. The Guard-captain of the trader's outpost is said to reward those able to rid Norcrofts of its Uruk enemies.\n",
[8415]="700087A3\n1\tReturn the meat to Mazauk\030Collect Morningthaw-haunches (total: 40)\tMorningthaw-bears can be found throughout the Ettenmoors. Mazauk directed you to get meat from the Morningthaw bears.\n",
[8416]="7002EEF5\n1\tDefeat Bûrzthrâng\tBûrzthrâng can be found somewhere within the ruins of Thornhope. Thane Béortnoth has asked you to slay Bûrzthrâng, the uruk who slew his father.\n2\tTalk to Thane Béortnoth outside Thornhope\tThane Béortnoth is encamped outside the walls of Thornhope. You should return to Béortnoth with the tidings that Bûrzthrâng is dead.\n",
})
